# Vue UI

- `<script setup lang="ts">`. Reuse `src/components/ui/` before adding one-off controls.
- Viewport WebGL stays in `Viewport3D.vue`. Other panels dispatch `editorCommands` or call stores.
- Bind tools to existing menus (`HeaderMenu`, `LeftToolbar`, command palette) and `keymapStore` when the user should see the shortcut.
- Do not copy `meshes` into local reactive state for editing; mutate through the project store so undo and the viewport stay aligned.
- Tailwind classes + current theme CSS variables (`themeStore`). No new component library.
- Icons: `BlenderIcon` first (`docs/ICONS.md`). Lucide only when no Blender glyph exists and the control is not a tool.
- Views: RMB pans (`docs/INPUT.md`). Do not add a canvas context menu.
